{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "status": "implemented_in_core_data",
  "disclaimer": "Source of truth for the legal and underground career contracts (D-049..D-053). scripts/generate_regional_content.py turns it into schema-3 work orders. A skill id must exist in rpg-core/src/main/resources/data/underground_city/skill_trees, a buyer id in .../buyers. Underground contracts need an underground buyer; legal contracts never carry trust or heat. Mod IDs are optional: an order that needs a missing mod is skipped at load, never an error.",
  "economy_rules": {
    "legal_margin": [
      1.3,
      2.1
    ],
    "underground_nominal_margin": [
      1.9,
      2.2
    ],
    "note": "Margins apply where every requirement is priced: credits / purchase cost of the consumed goods. Underground work pays more on paper (1.9-2.2x against 1.3-2.1x, and far larger absolute sums) because the goods must cross checkpoints, the buyer's demand is tiny and a seizure loses the goods and pays a fine. An errand (no contraband carried, the risk is only the buyer's trust) uses the legal band. scripts/validate_underground_balance.py computes the risk-adjusted result along the real corridor gates: careless smuggling must lose to legal work, a trained smuggler may beat it modestly, and nothing, not even a fully licensed carrier, may exceed twice the legal return."
  },
